A second review of the db-check changes upheld five findings in this
branch's code, all fixed here.

- The gate's needle had no left boundary, so a route calling a lookalike
  such as noterp.assert_permitted( counted as gated. This predates the
  branch. The call is now matched standing alone, after a character that
  cannot continue an identifier, as PostgreSQL's scanner defines one.
- A route that sets standard_conforming_strings off makes the scanner read
  \' inside any string as a quote, which the stripping cannot follow: a
  mention then reads as a call. Such a route is now reported whatever its
  body. No route sets it.
- The gated probe's identifier trap could not catch the misreading it named,
  because its apostrophe paired with others before the call. The identifier
  now sits on the call's own line. A lone double quote in a comment before
  it also catches a stripper that reads identifiers before comments and
  strings.
- fail() exited from inside the try, so the finally that stops the scratch
  cluster never ran: a migration or seed that failed to apply, or a control
  naming a missing assertion, left a postmaster running. fail() now stops
  the cluster first. That is checked on both paths: exit 1, and no
  postmaster left.
- The reader's comment said psql prints whitespace as an empty line; it
  prints only NULL and '' that way, and the old reader's trim() did the
  rest. A separator inside a value also split it into two rows. It is now
  read as a space, and the blank control holds one.

The same review found the CI runner change that follows from ubuntu-latest
moving to Ubuntu 26.04. That is not this branch's, and is kept apart.

Thirteen copies of the tree each reverted one piece, and db:check failed
with exactly the matching control. The thirteen pieces:
- 0025;
- the old public query;
- the raw strpos;
- the line-based reader;
- comments stripped before strings;
- no identifier branch;
- a comment ending only at a newline;
- the btrim wrapper;
- the needle without its boundary;
- no report for the setting;
- no separator replacement;
- identifiers read last;
- identifiers read first.

These pass:
- npm run db:check (133);
- db:fixtures;
- every pgTAP suite but 040;
- verify (695 tests);
- secret:scan;
- dep:policy.

Requirements: CAP-P04 · SEC-006

